    {
      "name": "Business Overview",
      "id": "05cce40c-cecc-41fa-95b7-60b257b5713b",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -280
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## PHASE 01 | Compact deterministic workflow\nUpload or run the readonly Gmail test batch. All business stages are inline. Python owns source isolation, originals/OCR, extraction cache and cooldown, validation, review tasks and notification delivery. Historical v5 is preserved.",
        "width": 2500,
        "height": 180
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Current Scope",
      "id": "51098db6-9207-48e4-be35-fbbdfea8ab73",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        490
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Current extractor, NOT an agent\nExtract Invoice Fields uses the existing Gemini structured extractor. LangChain Agent is a future step. Backend stage results share a persisted run_id contract; failed/skipped stages pass through without model calls. Failures are recorded immediately, before Record Exception.\n\nNotify Reviewer sends only to local Mailpit. Sent/unknown/in-flight notifications are not resent automatically. No approval, rejection, export, mailbox deletion or external sending. Export is inactive; bind the existing Gmail readonly credential after import on another instance.",
        "width": 2500,
        "height": 230
      }
    }
